{"from": "AC-2.12", "type": "refines", "to": "N-000160", "provenance": "judgment", "judgment": "J-003384", "rationale": "AC-2.12 specifies a concrete status derivation rule (priority ordering: conflict > ambiguous > stale > unchecked > validated), while N-000160 states the general principle that status is derived from facts and never stored independently.", "quotes": ["status follows conflict > ambiguous > stale > unchecked > validated", "Status is derived from facts, never stored independently"]}
{"from": "AC-2.12", "type": "subsumes", "to": "N-000693", "provenance": "judgment", "judgment": "J-002965", "rationale": "A specifies the complete status hierarchy (conflict > ambiguous > stale > unchecked > validated) with specific conditions; B only states that status is derived to `conflict` in F6, which is one instance already covered by A's hierarchy.", "quotes": ["for every combination of the four facts, status follows conflict > ambiguous > stale > unchecked > validated", "which derives their status to `conflict`"]}
